WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:06.000
Game of Thrones Season 7 Episode 5 begins
with Jaime washing ashore like Aragorn in

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.660
Two Towers, but instead of a sexy dream elf
to wake him, he’s got Bronn – “Listen

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:11.660
to me, cunt”.

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:16.269
Bronn points out the obvious – the Lannisters
can’t beat Daenerys with her three dragons,

00:00:16.269 --> 00:00:20.220
so Jaime goes to Cersei and says they can’t
win this war.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.730
But Cersei won’t surrender.

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:26.109
She says there’s too much bad blood to make
peace – Cersei won’t forgive Tyrion for

00:00:26.109 --> 00:00:31.810
killing her father Tywin, Dany won’t forgive
Jaime for killing her father Aerys, and Cersei

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:35.230
refuses to let go of the Iron Throne.

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:40.340
Tyrion Lannister walks through the ashes of
his family’s army – he seems to feel some

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.410
regret.

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:46.820
Then again, Tyrion did promise Cersei that
one day he’d turn her joy to ashes . Perhaps

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:51.460
that day has come – Tyrion turned Cersei’s
power to dust.

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:56.750
The Lannister army was also the pride of Tyrion’s
hated father Tywin . Maybe Tyrion feels some

00:00:56.750 --> 00:01:01.280
satisfaction wiping the last trace of his
father’s legacy.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:05.330
Daenerys tells the surviving Lannisters that
she’s not there to burn or murder, and then

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:09.630
she murders Randyll and Dickon by burning
them in front of their men.

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:12.490
Tyrion’s worried that this sends mixed messages.

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:17.229
Good leaders sometimes have to kill disloyal
lords – Robb and Jon both did.

00:01:17.229 --> 00:01:22.259
But burning a father and son alive reminds
people of Dany’s father Mad Aerys, who killed

00:01:22.259 --> 00:01:24.010
Rickard and Brandon Stark.

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:28.619
It’s a delicate balance between being a
strong leader and looking like a terrible

00:01:28.619 --> 00:01:32.729
tyrant, especially with the memory of Aerys
hanging over you.

00:01:32.729 --> 00:01:36.749
Dany talks about making the world better,
and breaking the wheel – a metaphor for

00:01:36.749 --> 00:01:41.579
stopping the cycle of conflict in Westeros
, and changing the political system – somehow.

00:01:41.579 --> 00:01:45.619
It’s not really clear what kind of changes
Dany wants to make.

00:01:45.619 --> 00:01:49.319
Remember, this is her first day on the Westerosi
mainland.

00:01:49.319 --> 00:01:54.279
She’s a stranger to this country, she doesn’t
know its problems – so how can she hope

00:01:54.279 --> 00:01:57.100
to reshape society for the better?

00:01:57.100 --> 00:02:01.210
Look at what she did in Meereen – she came
to a foreign city, destroyed its social structure,

00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:05.310
banned slavery, made herself queen, and tried
to make everything fair.

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:06.849
And – it was a disaster.

00:02:06.849 --> 00:02:11.650
The Sons of the Harpy revolted, the slavers
attacked in force, and Dany ended up leaving

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:13.820
with Daario in charge.

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:17.400
Since we haven’t heard any updates from
Daario’s Democratic Republic of the Bay

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:22.260
of Dragons lately, it’s probably fair to
assume things have turned bad in Meereen – just

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:27.420
like they did in Astapor and Yunkai . The
point is – Dany’s speech may be good political

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:28.420
rhetoric.

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:32.360
But we know ruling Westeros won’t be so
simple.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:36.980
Dany returns to Dragonstone, and Jon has a
moment with her dragon Drogon.

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:41.220
In the books, it’s hinted that dragons tend
to be more friendly to people who have Targaryen

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:46.620
blood – so maybe Drogon is nice to Jon because
Jon is the son of Rhaegar Targaryen.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:51.120
Then again, the dragons were also cool with
Tyrion, and he’s not a Targaryen – probably

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:54.760
– so this might not necessarily mean a whole
lot.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:59.300
Dany asks again about Jon’s death, and Jon
avoids the question again.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:03.060
Dany’s gonna have to find out about Jon’s
resurrection sometime.

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:07.450
She’s had magical rebirth or two herself,
so she’d probably understand.

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:12.410
Dany and Jon are fire and ice, and sometime
they gotta recognise it.

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:17.030
They’re interrupted by the arrival of Jorah,
now healed of his greyscale.

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:20.540
Dany and Jorah have a long and complex history.

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:24.530
Dany exiled Jorah in Season 4 for reporting
on her to Varys.

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:28.370
He returned to her briefly in Season 5 but
she didn’t forgive him for a while, they

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:33.750
reunited in Season 6, but Jorah had greyscale
so he went got cured, and now, he’s back

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:35.270
once again.

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:40.570
Jorah loves Dany, and in the books, this comes
off as creepy – Dany’s a teenager, and

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:45.270
Jorah’s this fugly middle-aged man who hits
on her cause she looks like his ex-wife . But,

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:49.560
still, Jorah has stayed loyal to Dany longer
than anyone else has.

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:53.760
They’ve been through a lot together, so
Dany wants him by her side.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:58.150
In the north, Bran uses his magic powers to
take control of a bunch of ravens.

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:02.330
He flies them over the Wall and looks at the
army of the dead, until the Night King seems

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:04.550
to break Bran’s control.

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:09.340
If the Night King can break Bran’s control
of ravens, could Bran break the Night King’s

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:11.340
control of these zombies?

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:14.160
Just deactivate the whole army of the dead
at once?

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:15.250
That’d be handy.

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:18.709
But we still don’t know how this magic works.

00:04:18.709 --> 00:04:22.850
It does seem that Bran and the Night King
use a similar kind of magic.

00:04:22.850 --> 00:04:27.580
Which might suggest that this human who became
the Night King years ago was originally a

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:30.210
greenseer, like Bran and Bloodraven.

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:35.880
In the books, Bran sees a vision of the bones
of other dreamers impaled on ice – maybe

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:41.240
the other white walkers were originally greenseers
who turned to the icy dark side of old gods

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:43.710
magic under Night King Darth Vader…

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:45.260
Or something.

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:48.930
After all this time, the walkers are still
super mysterious, so it’ll be awesome to

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:52.970
find out more about what they are and what
they want.

00:04:52.970 --> 00:04:58.120
Bran sees that the walkers are marching on
Eastwatch, the easternmost castle on the Wall.

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:03.840
Emphasis on the Wall – Eastwatch is behind
it, and the Wall is protected with magic which

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:07.720
apparently stops the dead getting through
– so they prolly can’t just bash down

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:09.520
the gate with an undead giant.

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:12.700
How, then, will the walkers pass the Wall?

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:16.800
In the opening credits of past episodes, the
ocean by the Wall has looked frozen-over,

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:21.830
so some people think they could maybe just
walk around atop the sea, or maybe do an underwater

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:23.750
Pirates of the Caribbean thing.

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:27.730
It probably would have been easier, though,
for the dead to go west instead.

00:05:27.730 --> 00:05:32.100
Cause to the west, the Wall ends, and there’s
a bridge across a gorge.

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:33.590
Why not cross there?

00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:37.110
The walkers must have some special plan to
get past Eastwatch.

00:05:37.110 --> 00:05:40.530
So Bran sends out letters to warn everyone.

00:05:40.530 --> 00:05:44.580
Down at the Citadel, the maesters want to
see evidence before they freak out about magic

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:45.580
zombies.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:49.480
Which in the real world would be very reasonable
– but in fantasy, sceptics are wrong.

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:53.980
The maesters mention other prophets from the
past, like Jenny of Oldstones.

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:58.950
Jenny was a mysterious common woman who married
a Targaryen prince bout fifty years ago.

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:02.730
Jenny was friends with a witch now known as
“the ghost of High Heart”, who said that

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:07.810
the prince that was promised, or Azor Ahai,
would be born of the line of Aerys and Rhaella

00:06:07.810 --> 00:06:12.070
– which means that either Daenerys or Jon
could be the hero to save the world – looks

00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:14.760
like Jenny was probably right.

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:17.520
The maesters also mention a guy called Lodos.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:21.460
Three hundred years ago, when the Targaryens
took the Iron Islands, Lodos claimed he was

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:26.590
the son of the Drowned God, and that krakens
would rise up to destroy Aegon’s fleet.

00:06:26.590 --> 00:06:30.280
That didn’t happen, and Lodos led a mass
suicide.

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:34.850
But in the books krakens have been seen recently
, and it’s looking like book-Euron might

00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:40.760
just turn himself some kinda Cthulu, so maybe
even Lodos was onto something.

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:45.400
Point is, both of the archmaesters’ examples
of prophecy being wrong might actually have

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:49.990
elements of truth – but they still don’t
believe in white walkers.

00:06:49.990 --> 00:06:54.250
This frustrates Sam so much that he abandons
his dream of becoming a maester, steals some

00:06:54.250 --> 00:06:57.560
books, and heads north to somehow help in
the war for the dawn.

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:01.750
He presumably brings the sword Heartsbane
with him – Sam’s father Randyll won’t

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:02.750
be needing it any more.

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:07.290
There’s not much love lost between Randyll
and Sam – but Dickon seemed alright, so

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:10.610
Sam might mourn the loss of his brother.

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:15.430
Before Sam leaves though, Gilly quietly drops
the biggest revelation in the season.

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:20.010
She reads in a book that a septon annulled
the marriage of Prince ‘Ragger’ and married

00:07:20.010 --> 00:07:25.800
him to someone else in a secret ceremony in
Dorne . What this means is that Prince Rhaegar

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:31.330
Targaryen – Daenerys’ older brother – set
aside his marriage to Elia Martell and secretly

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:36.300
married Lyanna Stark, who gave birth to Jon
Snow in Dorne.

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:39.860
Fans have speculated for years that something
like this had happened, cause this means that

00:07:39.860 --> 00:07:42.360
Jon Snow is not really a bastard.

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:47.330
He’s the legitimate child of Prince Rhaegar,
making him the legitimate heir of King Aerys,

00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:51.169
meaning Jon Snow should be King of Westeros.

00:07:51.169 --> 00:07:56.360
This complicates the situation with Jon’s
aunt Daenerys, who also claims the Throne.

00:07:56.360 --> 00:08:00.410
No one in the story knows all of this though
– so we’ll have to wait until Bran or

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:02.419
someone figures it out.

00:08:02.419 --> 00:08:07.440
At Dragonstone, Tyrion and Varys worry that
Dany might become a bad ruler like her father

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:12.090
Aerys – and Varys doesn’t quite know what
to do about this.

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:14.370
Varys used to seem so powerful.

00:08:14.370 --> 00:08:19.960
A secretive schemer, spymaster and Spider,
who knew everything and made everyone his

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:24.660
puppet . But now that he’s revealed his
hand, and made his loyalties clear, Varys

00:08:24.660 --> 00:08:28.630
is just a bald guy in a dressing gown hoping
for the best.

00:08:28.630 --> 00:08:35.710
He did always say that power is an illusion
. Jon and Dany and Tyrion work out a plan.

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:40.130
Jon will lead a team beyond the Wall to capture
a zombie, and bring it down to King’s Landing

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:45.100
to show Cersei, so that Cersei will help them
or at least not attack them or something when

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:48.240
they go back north to fight the dead.

00:08:48.240 --> 00:08:50.370
And this plan is… bad.

00:08:50.370 --> 00:08:55.170
It’s a huge risk to King Jon, and he’s
the guy uniting the north and the wildlings

00:08:55.170 --> 00:08:56.440
and Daenerys.

00:08:56.440 --> 00:09:00.730
And if they succeed in catching a zombie,
there’s no guarantee it’ll stay animated

00:09:00.730 --> 00:09:02.000
on the long journey south.

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:07.130
It might rot, or get out of range of the walkers’
magic, or just stop moving.

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:12.110
Even if all that works, all they’d achieve
is to show Cersei a zombie.

00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:16.899
Why would she be impressed, when she’s already
got a zombie, the Mountain.

00:09:16.899 --> 00:09:20.960
One zombie doesn’t prove the threat of the
army of the dead.

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:25.089
Even if Cersei does believe it, does anyone
really think Cersei would make peace with

00:09:25.089 --> 00:09:27.770
her enemies for the sake of the greater good?

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:30.630
Even if she does, what will her help be worth?

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:35.220
Dany just roasted a Lannister army, how many
men can Cersei have left?

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:39.560
How useful will soldiers be against the army
of the dead anyway?

00:09:39.560 --> 00:09:44.020
The best way to beat the dead would surely
be Dany’s dragons – why not fly up and

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:45.200
burn them all now?

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:49.570
Or if you just want to capture a zombie, why
not swoop down with a dragon and just grab

00:09:49.570 --> 00:09:50.570
one?

00:09:50.570 --> 00:09:55.500
The answer, of course, is the same reason
the eagles don’t fly Frodo to Mount Doom.

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:58.210
It’d be too easy, and too quick.

00:09:58.210 --> 00:10:02.440
But part of what makes Game of Thrones special,
and different to fantasies like Lord of the

00:10:02.440 --> 00:10:06.910
Rings, is that behind all the dragons and
zombies, there’s usually a strong logic

00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:08.209
to the plot.

00:10:08.209 --> 00:10:10.220
People make decisions that make sense.

00:10:10.220 --> 00:10:15.310
And this convoluted, dangerous, probably pointless
plan – does not make sense.

00:10:15.310 --> 00:10:20.420
At Winterfell, the lords of the north and
the Vale speak in support of Sansa.

00:10:20.420 --> 00:10:24.300
It almost sounds like they want to declare
her their Queen , when only last season they

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:25.860
declared Jon their King.

00:10:25.860 --> 00:10:30.980
Before that, they mostly supported the Boltons,
and before that Robb Stark.

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:34.760
Seems they can’t go a season without wanting
to switch sides.

00:10:34.760 --> 00:10:39.730
Arya accuses Sansa of undermining Jon, and
wanting power for herself.

00:10:39.730 --> 00:10:42.779
Sansa tries to be reasonable, but Arya just
won’t listen.

00:10:42.779 --> 00:10:47.460
It makes sense that Arya doesn’t get the
politics – she’s spent seasons training

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:50.360
with assassins, not learning diplomacy.

00:10:50.360 --> 00:10:53.510
But this seems rooted in something deeper
for Arya.

00:10:53.510 --> 00:10:58.260
She criticises Sansa for loving pretty things
and feeling superior , which connects to the

00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:03.450
jealousy and resentment Arya had for Sansa
growing up – over how Sansa was perfect

00:11:03.450 --> 00:11:06.330
and pretty, while Arya never fit.

00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:10.760
Maybe the real reason for Arya’s aggression
is all this old anger.

00:11:10.760 --> 00:11:14.050
Whatever the reason, Littlefinger sees an
opportunity.

00:11:14.050 --> 00:11:18.959
He manipulates Arya into finding the old letter
that Cersei made Sansa write supporting King

00:11:18.959 --> 00:11:21.390
Joffrey and condemning the Starks.

00:11:21.390 --> 00:11:25.540
This wasn’t really Sansa’s fault – she
was just a kid, she had no real choice.

00:11:25.540 --> 00:11:30.100
But this might work as a way for Petyr to
isolate Sansa from the rest of her family

00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:34.800
– to create chaos and division which he
can use to gain more influence.

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:40.260
This is some classic Petyr Baelish evil scheming,
and in the short term, it much just work.

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:44.300
But in the long term, Sansa can just explain
how she was forced to write the letter, Arya

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:49.010
can figure out that Petyr misled her, and
Bran can reveal he’s magically seen every

00:11:49.010 --> 00:11:51.200
evil thing that Petyr’s ever done.

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:55.630
So Littlefinger’s fucked – but at least
he gets one last lurk in.

00:11:55.630 --> 00:12:00.100
Tyrion and Davos arrive at King’s Landing,
and Davos mentions the death of his son Matthos

00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:01.670
in Season 2.

00:12:01.670 --> 00:12:05.870
Davos has a wife and kids back home, and he
often thinks about them in the books . But

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:09.940
while everyone else complains about their
personal drama all the time, Davos usually

00:12:09.940 --> 00:12:13.600
keeps things to himself, and carries on his
duty.

00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:16.339
But he remembers his friends.

00:12:16.339 --> 00:12:21.020
Davos goes and meets with Gendry, the bastard
son of King Robert who was last seen rowing

00:12:21.020 --> 00:12:24.320
in Season 3 after Melisandre tried to burn
him.

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:29.600
Gendry wields a warhammer, just like his father
did, decorated with the stag of his house.

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:34.740
It looks like Gendry identifies with his father’s
family, the Baratheons – maybe after the

00:12:34.740 --> 00:12:40.270
war is won, he’ll rule the Baratheon seat
of Storm’s End – since every other Baratheon

00:12:40.270 --> 00:12:41.330
is dead.

00:12:41.330 --> 00:12:44.810
As the son of King Robert, though, Gendry
could also potentially have a claim on the

00:12:44.810 --> 00:12:50.470
Iron Throne – which, as Davos says, complicates
the situation with Jon and Dany.

00:12:50.470 --> 00:12:52.810
Meanwhile, Tyrion goes to meet Jaime.

00:12:52.810 --> 00:12:56.810
Tyrion tries to justify his killing of their
father Tywin, but Jaime doesn’t want to

00:12:56.810 --> 00:12:59.480
hear it, and threatens to kill Tyrion.

00:12:59.480 --> 00:13:04.120
The brothers’ relationship in the books
is even worse – they parted on bad terms,

00:13:04.120 --> 00:13:07.290
with Tyrion lying and saying he killed Joffrey.

00:13:07.290 --> 00:13:11.149
So their reunion in the books might be a lot
darker.

00:13:11.149 --> 00:13:15.410
Anyway Tyrion gets to the point and asks Jaime
to convince Cersei to peacefully meet with

00:13:15.410 --> 00:13:17.050
Dany and Jon.

00:13:17.050 --> 00:13:18.269
On the way out, Davos and co.

00:13:18.269 --> 00:13:20.290
have some trouble with gold cloaks.

00:13:20.290 --> 00:13:25.730
It really was a big risk coming here in broad
daylight with the recognisable Imp – they

00:13:25.730 --> 00:13:29.050
all could easily have been caught and killed
by Cersei.

00:13:29.050 --> 00:13:32.790
But Gendry solves their problems with his
hammer, and they get away.

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:38.400
Jaime reveals to Cersei that he met Tyrion,
and Cersei reveals to Jaime she already knew,

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:40.040
and allowed it to happen.

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:41.510
Which is pretty surprising.

00:13:41.510 --> 00:13:45.030
Cersei hates and fears Tyrion more than anyone
else in the world.

00:13:45.030 --> 00:13:49.270
You’d think she’d take the chance to kill
him . But apparently, Cersei’s decided she

00:13:49.270 --> 00:13:52.920
needs to make peace with Daenerys to beat
her in the long run.

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:57.700
Cersei tells Jaime that she’s pregnant,
and the twins share an emotional moment, which

00:13:57.700 --> 00:14:03.040
Cersei immediately exploits to tell Jaime
to never betray her . So this is some classic

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:08.330
emotional manipulation from Cersei, using
a tender moment for strategic gain.

00:14:08.330 --> 00:14:11.279
But there’s probably also some sincerity
here.

00:14:11.279 --> 00:14:15.269
Cersei’s pregnancy might help explain why
Cersei went from wanting to fight to the death

00:14:15.269 --> 00:14:18.060
to wanting peace within one episode.

00:14:18.060 --> 00:14:19.730
She has a child to protect now.

00:14:19.730 --> 00:14:22.700
But the pregnancy also raises questions.

00:14:22.700 --> 00:14:26.510
Maggy the Frog predicted that Cersei would
have three children – a fourth child would

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:28.670
go against that prophecy.

00:14:28.670 --> 00:14:32.910
In the show, Cersei did have a short-lived
baby with Robert , so maybe that number’s

00:14:32.910 --> 00:14:33.950
out the window anyway.

00:14:33.950 --> 00:14:37.980
But it still would be weird if Cersei had
another child.

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:42.980
Maybe she’ll die before it’s born – but
if the valonqar theory is true and Jaime kills

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:47.510
Cersei, would he kill his own unborn child
along with his twin?

00:14:47.510 --> 00:14:49.890
This baby raises the stakes.

00:14:49.890 --> 00:14:52.550
At Dragonstone, Jon meets Gendry.

00:14:52.550 --> 00:14:57.589
Gendry’s father Robert, and Jon’s supposed
father Ned were close friends, and their bond

00:14:57.589 --> 00:15:00.410
inspires a friendship between Gendry and Jon.

00:15:00.410 --> 00:15:04.899
Gendry’s keen to join the fight against
the dead, which is a little surprising given

00:15:04.899 --> 00:15:10.420
he has no experience with white walkers or
the north – but Gendry has seen some mystical

00:15:10.420 --> 00:15:14.930
shit, what with Beric and the red witch, so
it’s plausible enough he believes in the

00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:18.310
dead – if it gives him something to swing
at.

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:23.130
Tyrion farewells Jorah, and hints at their
rocky past – remember that one time Jorah

00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:24.910
dwarfnapped Tyrion?

00:15:24.910 --> 00:15:29.480
And Dany farewells Jorah for the umpteenth
time – maybe the last time.

00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:32.880
And finally Dany farewells Jon with a longing
gaze.

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:37.050
It’d save a lot of hassle if these guys
just admitted that they wanna bone, cause

00:15:37.050 --> 00:15:41.530
a marriage alliance between Dany and Jon would
be hugely powerful – it’d clear up the

00:15:41.530 --> 00:15:46.670
problem of their competing claims on the Throne
– they could rule together as King and Queen.

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:50.410
Chuck Gendry in there for a threesome, and
you’d solve the whole succession crisis

00:15:50.410 --> 00:15:51.410
in one go.

00:15:51.410 --> 00:15:54.360
But might have to leave that for the fanfic.

00:15:54.360 --> 00:15:58.899
At Eastwatch, Jon forms the greatest squad
of warriors Westeros has ever seen.

00:15:58.899 --> 00:16:03.670
There’s Jon Snow – the white wolf, the
resurrected King in the North.

00:16:03.670 --> 00:16:06.279
Gendry, “the Bull”, bastard son of King
Robert.

00:16:06.279 --> 00:16:11.240
Thoros – the “red wizard” of Myr, and
Beric Dondarrion – the Lightning Lord, six

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:12.589
times reborn.

00:16:12.589 --> 00:16:16.730
There’s Jorah Mormont, Ser Friendzone, survivor
of greyscale.

00:16:16.730 --> 00:16:21.880
Tormund Giantsbane, “Husband to Bears”,
“Mead-King of Ruddy Hall” . And Sandor

00:16:21.880 --> 00:16:25.660
Clegane – the Hound, gravedigger, eater
of chicken.

00:16:25.660 --> 00:16:29.260
It’s an amazing team, which ordinarily would
be impossible.

00:16:29.260 --> 00:16:33.920
Cause these guys are knights and wildlings,
northerners and southerners, followers of

00:16:33.920 --> 00:16:37.850
the old gods and of R’hllor – there’s
a lot of bad blood.

00:16:37.850 --> 00:16:40.850
Gendry was sold to Melisandre by Thoros and
Beric.

00:16:40.850 --> 00:16:43.959
Beric was killed by the Hound then resurrected.

00:16:43.959 --> 00:16:48.240
Tormund’s people were hunted and killed
by Jorah’s father Jeor Moment.

00:16:48.240 --> 00:16:50.870
Any other time, these guys would be enemies.

00:16:50.870 --> 00:16:55.990
But because of the threat of the dead, none
of these grudges matter any more . Which kind

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:58.329
of says it all about this new season.

00:16:58.329 --> 00:17:02.850
There’s no time for the complexity, the
history, or the logistics – the story is

00:17:02.850 --> 00:17:05.610
hurtling towards its climax.

00:17:05.610 --> 00:17:11.300
There is something lost when the show moves
so fast – but it is fucken fun to watch.

00:17:11.300 --> 00:17:15.650
The heroes step beyond the Wall to face the
night.

00:17:15.650 --> 00:17:20.140
This scene when Cersei made Sansa write a
letter against the Starks is a really interesting

00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:22.540
chapter of the Game of Thrones books.

00:17:22.540 --> 00:17:27.799
It shows how naïve and trusting Sansa once
was, and how manipulative Cersei is, using

00:17:27.799 --> 00:17:32.490
love to assure loyalty – just like she does
with Jaime this episode.

